Lab patch 0002: one model client per run, tagged with its agent
(agentic/orchestrator_helpers/llm_setup.py).

Why, part 1: apply_project_settings() turns patch 0001's SettingsUnavailable into
llm_setup_failure, so the orchestrator ends the run with a non-recoverable error
frame (code settings_unavailable) instead of a traceback or a default model.

Why, part 2: the LLM tap stores request bodies but no headers, and RedAmon's
fireteam members share one client. Each OpenAI-compatible request now carries the
standard OpenAI "user" field "redamon:<purpose>:<agent>", read from the
current_llm_purpose ContextVar upstream already sets at every call site and the
member scope of fireteam_deploy_node. The adapter's agent_ids() reads it from the
tap's NNNN.req.json. The model never sees the field.

